# Domain value objects

Files under `backend/src/shared/domain/values/` are DDD **value objects**, not DTO shapes.

Follow `user-email.ts`:

- `export class Foo extends ValueObject<FooProps>`
- props interface is a private construction shape, not the public type
- `private constructor` + `public static create(...): Result<Foo>`
- getters for fields; equality via `ValueObject.equals`

```ts
// BAD — interface in values/ is a DTO, not a value object
export interface GoogleAuthTokens {
  accessToken: string;
  refreshToken: string;
}

// GOOD
export class GoogleAuthTokens extends ValueObject<GoogleAuthTokensProps> {
  private constructor(props: GoogleAuthTokensProps) {
    super(props);
  }
  public static create(props: GoogleAuthTokensProps): Result<GoogleAuthTokens> { /* Guard + Result */ }
}
```

Passport/HTTP payloads stay in infra (e.g. `GoogleOAuthTokenPayload`). Map them to the value object in the use-case with `Foo.create(...)`.
